oyl (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * oyl_upgrade: a YAML 1.1 file made YAML 1.2 in place. Only what a
    1.2 reader reads otherwise is rewritten, the rest kept byte for byte,
    and each change reported; the output is checked in the file's reader
    and in YAML 1.2 before it is returned.
  * The YAML 1.1 and go-yaml v2 dialects read a quoted scalar's or flow
    collection's lines not indented past their block, as libyaml does,
    with a warning (OYL_SYNTAX_FLOW_INDENT).
  * Seven fixes to YAML 1.2 parsing, found by comparing with PyYAML,
    go-yaml v2 and the yaml package and by fuzzing the upgrade: a tab
    after a line break counted as indentation, a key's ':' on the next
    line, two tags or anchors on one node, a repeated block header
    indicator, empty lines in flow and after an escaped line break, and
    marks after an escaped lone CR. Input Oyl read wrongly is now an
    error, or read right.
  * API and ABI compatible with 1.0: the runtime library is still
    liboyl.so.1.

 -- Thomas Sawyer <transfire@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:52:08 -0400

oyl (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Windows: builds with MSVC on x64, 32-bit x86 and ARM64, tested in CI.
  * Parsing up to 2.8x as fast as 1.2.0, ahead of rapidyaml's event
    parser on every benchmark input: fewer instructions per token, and
    fast paths for one-line flow collections and plain key: value lines.
  * An anchor or tag on a block node no longer hands the rest of the
    stream to the eager parser; invalid input with such properties now
    gets the events up to the error, and some flow errors read
    differently.
  * Float literals longer than 768 significant digits round exactly with
    any strtod, MSVC's included.
  * API and ABI compatible with 1.0: the runtime library is still
    liboyl.so.1.

 -- Thomas Sawyer <transfire@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:44:35 -0400

oyl (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Trees: oyl_parse_tree reads a document into one flat array of nodes,
    whose lookups follow aliases and apply merges, with keys compared as
    YAML compares them; oyl_emit_tree writes one back.
  * Scalar values (oyl_schema_value) and dialects, chosen per document by
    its directives: YAML 1.2, YAML 1.1 as PyYAML reads it, go-yaml v2 as
    Kubernetes reads it, and dialects a program builds.
  * oyl_parse_json: YAML to JSON, byte for byte as sigs.k8s.io/yaml with
    the go-yaml v2 dialect.
  * Emitter: 1.5-7x faster; checks the order of events; writes only what
    reads back; keeps documents' %YAML and %TAG directives.
  * Parser fixes found by fuzzing and code review; hash tables keyed
    against collision floods; running out of memory always reported.
  * API and ABI compatible with 1.0: the runtime library is still
    liboyl.so.1.

 -- Thomas Sawyer <transfire@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:53:00 -0400

oyl (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed from yam to oyl: the oyl_/OYL_ API prefix, <oyl/oyl.h>,
    liboyl, and the oyl source package.
  * First stable release. The ABI is now stable within 1.x; the runtime
    library is liboyl.so.1 (package liboyl1, replacing libyam0).
  * API: events and tokens are owned by the library and returned by const
    pointer; schemas are opaque; the emitter is configured with setters and
    gains oyl_emit_* builders. Only the public API is exported.
  * Conformance: all 308 valid YAML Test Suite cases parse to the expected
    events and all 94 invalid cases are rejected; emitted YAML parses back
    to the same data.
  * Safety limits on events, nesting depth and alias/merge expansion.
  * Faster parsing: flow/JSON about 1.7x, block and quoted scalars up to 5x.
  * Many parser and emitter fixes found by fuzzing.

 -- Thomas Sawyer <transfire@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:18:04 -0400

